        "text": "=Business: {{ $('All Leads').item.json['Business Name'] }}\nRating: {{ $('All Leads').item.json['Rating '] }}  from {{ $('All Leads').item.json['Review count'] }} reviews\nServices: {{ $('All Leads').item.json.Services }}\nHours: {{ $('Clean Data').item.json.hours }}\nNeighborhood: {{ $('All Leads').item.json.Location }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You write personalized opening lines for cold emails to local businesses.\nRules:\n- Write one to two sentences.\n- Use only the facts provided. Never invent details such as customer complaints or services.\n- Be warm and specific. No flattery clichés and no exclamation marks.\n- Do not mention what the sender sells.\n- If a fact is missing or empty, skip it and use another.\n- Return only the line, with no quotes or extra text.\n\n- Base the line on exactly one fact and put that fact in detail_used, with its numbers.\n- Copy ratings, review counts and hours exactly as given. Never round or guess.\n- Only mention opening hours if the Hours field is provided and non-empty.\n- Maximum 40 words, two sentences.\n\n\n- Start with \"Hi [business name] team,\".\n- Write ratings as \"5-star rating\" or \"4.8-star rating\", never \"a 5 from 20 reviews\".\n- Write the line as natural speech, as a friendly person would say it.\n- In detail_used, write plain text with no quotation marks, for example: 5-star rating from 20 reviews.\n\nExample of the style (do not copy the facts):\nHi Sample Spa team, a 4.9-star rating from 139 reviews is a great sign that clients trust you."
        }
      },
